      "title": "[P1] Keep the serialized MCP resource under the fetch budget",
      "body": "Adding these parsers leaves the single-file app at 978,810 raw bytes, but escaping that HTML into the JSON-RPC `resources/read` response produces roughly 1,007,825 bytes. That exceeds the 1,000,000-byte fetch budget documented by `scripts/check-mcp-app-bundle.mjs`, so hosts enforcing the limit on the resource response can again reject the template before iframe startup; measure and constrain the serialized payload or use a smaller renderer.",
