        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Retain a safe upper bound for chart heights",
      "body": "When an agent-authored `json_template` supplies a very large `height`, removing the previous upper clamp lets the SVG and MCP auto-resized iframe become arbitrarily tall, potentially stalling rendering or destroying the host layout. The same unbounded conversion was added to PieChart and StackedAreaChart; allow the required 400px contract while retaining a finite maximum.",
