        "absolute_file_path": "/Users/burakemre/Code/lobu/.claude/worktrees/mcp-app-prod-fetch/packages/owletto/src/mcp-apps/interaction/json-template-view.tsx",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 180,
          "end": 180
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Preserve date-only and categorical axis labels",
      "body": "For date-only rows such as `2026-08-09`, `new Date` interprets the value as UTC and `getDate()` displays 8/8 for users west of UTC; the permissive parser also converts fallback labels such as `Jan` into `1/1`. These stored labels were previously displayed verbatim, so parse only known timestamps using appropriate UTC semantics and leave arbitrary labels unchanged.",
      "confidence_score": 0.99,
      "priority": 2,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/Users/burakemre/Code/lobu/.claude/worktrees/mcp-app-prod-fetch/packages/owletto/src/mcp-apps/interaction/json-template-view.tsx",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 574,
          "end": 577
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Clamp a 100% range start to the final row",
      "body": "When Range start is dragged to 100% while Range end is also 100%, this calculation produces `rows.length`; the subsequent lookup is undefined and `onDateRangeSelect` is silently skipped even though the controls show a last-point range. Clamp the start index to `rows.length - 1`, as is already done for the end index.",
